.TH git-save "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset 0.156.0" "SMI Git Command"
.SH NAME
git-save \- show the state, commit all changes and push them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git save
\fIMESSAGE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBgit save\fR command saves the work of the current folder to the remote in one go:
.IP 1. 4
\fBgit state\fR: the branches and the working tree status, before anything is changed.
.IP 2. 4
\fBgit add .\fR: every change of the current folder and below it, new files included.
.IP 3. 4
\fBgit commit \-m\fR \fIMESSAGE\fR.
.IP 4. 4
\fBgit push\fR: to the push target of the current branch.
.PP
It stops on the first failing step, so nothing is pushed when there is nothing to commit or the commit
fails. The message is required and is one argument, so it is quoted when it has spaces.
.PP
Git runs it as a subcommand because the executable \fBgit-save\fR is in the \fBPATH\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIMESSAGE\fR
The commit message.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B git save \(dqparandasin harude skripti\(dq
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
